1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,090
Paid a scammer by

2
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:01,850
card?

3
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,390
Don't just cancel it.

4
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,550
Ask for this.

5
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:05,530
If you paid by

6
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,210
credit card, contact the

7
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,310
company that issued the

8
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,710
card right away.

9
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:10,670
Use the number on

10
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:11,330
the back of the

11
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,510
card, or log in

12
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:13,550
to your account.

13
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:14,450
Tell them it was

14
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,890
a fraudulent charge and

15
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,350
ask for a refund.

16
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,830
The FTC notes that

17
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,330
federal law protects you

18
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,830
from unauthorized use of

19
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,010
your credit card.

20
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,590
Debit card works the

21
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,290
same way.

22
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,790
Contact your bank or

23
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,190
credit union, use the

24
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:28,850
number on the back

25
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,790
of the card,

26
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,950
report it, and ask

27
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,070
for a refund.

28
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:33,690
The FTC says federal

29
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,470
protections apply to unauthorized

30
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,290
debit card use too.

